      "side": 1,
      "message": "I mainly wanted it somewhere that\u0027s convenient to find, which is why I didn\u0027t use mktemp. (It makes it easier to open the results in a visual diff viewer). It\u0027s not something people would normally run unless they were trying to compare builds. It\u0027s also not run as part of the build process or anything. I usually like to leave things like that out of .gitignore so they show up in my \"git status\", but I can add to .gitignore if that\u0027s preferable (to accidentally check it in someone would have to do \"git add maps\" and then \"git commit\". \"git commit -a\" wouldn\u0027t add a new directory).",
