      "writtenOn": "2019-02-19T23:29:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e What\u0027s the point of seeing it in \u0027git status\u0027 if this is something which does not affect the result of the build?\n\nMainly just because I like to know if my git directory is *really* clean without running \"git status --ignored\". I generally don\u0027t like to have unknown files lingering about when I\u0027m trying to do a \"clean\" build, though in this case it shouldn\u0027t affect the build. It\u0027s mainly just paranoia and personal preference.\n\nPutting it in the build directory should work.",
